diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 3d4c9ec8e..a06b5578b 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@ Some features are not supported in AdvCiv-SAS; e.g., non-English languages, pre-
 - **C++ inline-return cleanup:** collapsed simple inline DLL header functions whose bodies were exactly one `return` statement to one physical line, making trivial getters/wrappers easier to grep and compare. Done with the help of [`collapse_cpp_inline_returns.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#collapse_cpp_inline_returnspy), a conservative mechanical helper that skips constructors/destructors, multi-statement bodies, body comments, multiline signatures, and overlong results. For example, `int getGoldPerTurnByPlayer(PlayerTypes ePlayer) const { return m_aiGoldPerTurnByPlayer.get(ePlayer); } // Exposed to Python`, instead of its old four-line equivalent.
 - **Build cleanup - disabled unneeded DLL test code in normal builds:** compile-gated disabled reproducibility-test code (`ReproTest.cpp`) so normal DLL builds no longer compile it unless explicitly enabled for debugging. This keeps dormant test/debug code out of normal builds, may slightly reduce DLL/build size, and does **not** change gameplay. Found with the help of the new [`find_cpp_dead_code_candidates.py`](/LLM_Helpers/find_cpp_dead_code_candidates.py) LLM/manual-review helper.
 - **GitHub workflow build checks:** added GitHub Actions checks under [`.github/workflows`](/.github/workflows/) to catch forgotten debug/default settings and data drift at each commit. Current checks notably verify launch-guard sentinel values, XML tag references in SAS define text values, integer SAS define bounds, valid main-menu opening-music script setup, disabled BBAI logging defaults, shared UI font defaults, Sevopedia Leader AI Personality Panel predumped-cache defaults and predump file presence, `WorldSizeTypes` enum/XML alignment, `CvGameCoreDLL/Project/temp_files/` staying effectively empty (only its tracked placeholder file), not being ignored by `.gitignore`, and being allowed only as an archive-excluded development marker through `.gitattributes` (helps catch stale fast-compile temp files. We check this because we suspect fast compiles can be unreliable, and also helps catch forgetting to replace the committed DLL after compiling; see [KI#38](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#38---no-idea-why-but-sometimes-compile-mysteriouslystrangelyinconsistently-fails-and-recompiling-succeeds-underwith-but-exact-same-source-files-if-i-am-not-mistaken-but) and [KI#38.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#382---weird-dll-xml-errors-at-launch-solved-by-recompiling-the-exact-same-dll-cosmic-ray-2-or-something-else-maybe-or-whatever-maybe-but)), and every playable `PrivateMaps/*.py` being listed exactly once across the SAS map-script heaviness/coverage defines while every listed map script exists in `PrivateMaps/`. For example, this helped spot [map scripts that were previously unclassified in SAS map-script heaviness defines](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27198308080/job/80295526028); they are now listed explicitly for exhaustiveness (more robust; no gameplay change).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6081+) **Civ4 GameText character check:** added a GitHub workflow check for Unicode typography that creates visible artifacts in Civ4 text, such as the em dash (`U+2014`) formerly used in the Automobiles Civilopedia instead of a simple hyphen or other ASCII punctuation. It also catches repeated question marks that indicate lost characters, while allowing readable accented letters and ignoring XML comments.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6081+) **Technology audio check:** added a GitHub workflow check that resolves every technology's normal and multiplayer audio through the mod-local audio tables and ensures each technology keeps a distinct spoken recording. This catches missing local definitions that otherwise produce quote text without audio, as happened with Drama, as well as wrong-layer script/sound references.
 - **AIP predump refresh bot:** added [`aip-predump-refresh.yml`](/.github/workflows/aip-predump-refresh.yml), a tested GitHub Actions bot workflow for the Sevopedia Leader AI Personality predump cache. The existing checker still fails when the committed predump is stale, but the refresh workflow can now run `aip_predump_values.py --write` outside Civ4 and open/update a bot PR containing only `SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py` when real generated AIP data or display-label drift is detected. It runs automatically after pushes to known AIP predump dependency files. Tested in [PR #31](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/31) with no-op, XML comment-only, numeric Leader XML, and Python label/display drift cases, so harmless comments do not refresh the cache while real generated predump changes do.
 - Other examples: This notably also **helped spot and fix duplicate text, parent, and child XML keys** found by new GitHub workflow check [text](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27332010214/job/80746523894), [parent](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27258698041/job/80498936912), and [child](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27336768909/job/80762873956) (See [KI#148](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#148---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-one-advciv-sas-issue-of-duplicate-parent-xml-keys-found-by-new-github-workflow-check), [KI#149](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#149---fixed-base-advciv-issue-duplicate-xml-text-tags-found-by-new-github-workflow-check), [KI#150](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#150---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-some-advciv-sas-priority-duplicate-xml-childlist-entries-found-by-new-github-workflow-check)), and [suspicious malformed-looking XML tag punctuation](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27342682844/job/80783239087) (e.g., `<French>>`, `</English>>`) (see [KI#151](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#151---fixed-base-advciv-issue-suspicious-malformed-looking-xml-angle-tags-found-by-new-github-workflow-check)) and [XML suspicious text chars](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27400470104/job/80977135402) (see [KI#152](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#152---fixed-suspicious-replacement-question-marks-in-lengthy-sevopedia-xml-found-by-new-github-workflow-check)). The checks also run locally with Python 3; see [`.github/workflows/README.md` current build checks](/.github/workflows/README.md#current-build-checks).
